These lemmas are **jointly 1-inductive** for `WIDTH >= 8`, assuming reset is asserted for at least one clock before checking the assertions. The width condition matters: at `WIDTH = 7`, assigning `-100` to `x` truncates it to `28`, so the module can enter `DONE` while `y` is still `-6`; the target property is then false. ([fpga.mit.edu](https://fpga.mit.edu/6205/_static/F25/documentation/1800-2017.pdf))

